dockerfile ? ---> has a set of instructions that will helps u to containeriz the application.
dockerfile components:-
1. From : used to define base images (Ex:- pyhton, mysql, nginx images )
2. Expose : used to expose the container Port ( Ex:- 80, 8080, 5000, 3000 )
3. Maintainer : Used to add author details ( Ex:- mustfa, manikanta, aruna, devi )
4. Labels : used to add a description about our images 
5. Copy : used to copy the files from host to container ( Syntax :- CP SOURCE DESTINATION ), it can't support url's. 
6. Add : used to copy the files from host to containers, also it supports url's And extract Zipfiles also 

COMMANDS:
to create an image : docker build -t imagename .
to create a container : docker run -itd --name cont-name imagename
to create a container : docker run -d --name contname -p portnumber (1111:80) imagename
to enter into container : docker exec -it cont-name bash



Example of Dockerfile based on above components:
FROM ubuntu
EXPOSE 80
MAINTAINER mustafa
LABELS this is my first image
COPY index.html .
ADD <url-from-internet> .
